			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Fix binary file corruption in FileProtocolShim\n\nThe file:read Tauri command was incorrectly invoked with named-object args ({ path, encoding: \"utf8\" }) and the response was assumed to be a string. Mountain actually returns raw bytes as { buffer: number[] } and ignores the encoding param entirely. When VS Code loaded binary files (WASM, fonts, images), the response body became \"[object Object]\" which corrupted the data.\n\nFix by:\n1) Invoking file:read with positional array args [path] as expected by MountainIPCInvoke\n2) Adding UnwrapReadResult() to unwrap { buffer: number[] } into Uint8Array for binary-safe Response bodies\n3) Updating content type to Uint8Array | string | Blob | null\n\nThis restores TextMate grammar loading and binary asset handling. All three protocol handlers (VSCodeFileHandler, VSCodeUserDataHandler, FileHandler) now use the binary-safe pattern.",
			"SHA": "7ef0dadbc290f5c380e157c18f6df72411d0b840"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:45:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 3 components\n\nSynchronize Mountain, Output, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n- **Mountain:** Add IsUserExtensionScanPath() helper to distinguish user extensions in ~/.land/extensions from bundled paths like Resources/extensions and VS Code's submodule. Previously all extensions were marked IsBuiltin=true regardless of source, causing user-installed VSIXes to appear under \"Built-in\" in the Extensions sidebar. Also expand v2.1 changelog with April 17–22 commits (documentation).\n- **Output:** Add CatchOutputFolderRejection transform plugin to silence harmless promise rejections from VS Code's outputServices.createFolder(). The VFS-IPC stat call rejects with FileNotFound before fileService handles it, causing telemetry noise in PostHog. The plugin appends .catch(() => undefined) to silence the rejection.\n- **Wind:** Add missing stub handlers in TauriMainProcessService for extension tips (empty arrays), MCP management (empty arrays), user data sync (status tuple), and language detection (empty extensions) to prevent renderer crashes.\n\nImpact: User VSIX extensions now appear correctly under \"Installed\" (not \"Built-in\"), renderer gracefully handles missing backends without crashes, and telemetry noise is reduced.",
			"SHA": "73b6871435a39151d1326301c3c1a332a3c58e85"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T23:21:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Land): Expand CHANGELOG Batch 1 — Mountain 2026-04-22",
			"SHA": "696d640c8a3f627b8f81d5258d1522e4a7cb06e1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T22:55:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Ensure extension manifest fields and type filtering work correctly\n\nFour related fixes address extension loading failures and missing activation:\n\n1. Manifest field serialization: Remove `skip_serializing_if` from Name, Version, Publisher fields. VS Code's trusted-publishers migration calls `manifest.publisher.toLowerCase()` at boot—if the key is omitted, the renderer crashes with `TypeError: undefined is not an object`. Add IPC handler hardening with explicit fallback values.\n\n2. Extension type filtering: Respect the ExtensionType filter passed to `getInstalled(type?)`. Previously all calls returned the full list as `type: 0, isBuiltin: true`. Now System extensions (type=0) and User extensions (type=1, including VSIX) are properly distinguished. Forward filters from `scanSystemExtensions` and `scanUserExtensions` handlers.\n\n3. Post-install activation: Fire `onStartupFinished` activation events after `$deltaExtensions` adds an extension. Without this, extensions like `Anthropic.claude-code` register but never activate—sidebar contributions silently no-op until restart.\n\n4. Log file eager init: Call `InitEager()` at binary startup to preserve logs before any panic. Fix `BinarySignature()` PascalCase splitting. Expand benign ENOENT ignore list.\n\nImpact: VSIX extensions now show under \"Installed\" with Uninstall, activate immediately after install without reload, and the Extensions sidebar refresh works correctly.",
			"SHA": "dd606e20bdc57b03917454d8b6a2fc9cc4563fc7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T22:18:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Add shutdown guard and fix static asset path resolution\n\nAdd atomic shutdown guard to Entry.rs to prevent the graceful shutdown sequence from running twice. The graceful path ends with `app_handle.exit(0)` which Tauri re-delivers as a second `ExitRequested { code: Some(0) }`. On re-entry we must NOT `prevent_exit` or spawn the shutdown task again — Cocoon has already been SIGKILLed and the second pass would log spurious \"tcp connect error\" warnings.\n\nExtend static asset path resolution in Utilities.rs to handle both `/Static/Application/` and `Static/Application/` forms. The webview's WASM loader resolves asset URLs relative to the current document, which strips the leading slash before reaching the `file:read` IPC handler. Without this fix, `tokio::fs::read` would fail with ENOENT, breaking TextMate syntax highlighting.\n\nAlso expand the benign ENOENT ignore list in DevLog.rs to suppress warnings for `.copilot/agents`, `.vscode/tasks.json`, `/User/tasks.json`, `/User/mcp.json`, `vscode-chat-images`, and `/output_<TIMESTAMP>` window log file patterns.\n\nThis prevents spurious shutdown warnings, fixes TextMate grammar loading, and reduces log noise.",
			"SHA": "bd38c344b6e75841edd53fa141b61eb9cb6a257b"
		}
	],
